{
  "about": "The Kodus egress lists (docs/runtime/egress-allowlist.md §7). One file for the API and the cell: the API refuses approving a denied host, the cell refuses it from every source (base list, approval, secret host). apps/runtime-cell/internal/netguard/egress-lists.json is a byte copy (go:embed); both sides test that it is identical and that their matcher gives every case below. A pattern's * stands for one or more host characters, dots included: *.ngrok.io is every name under ngrok.io, s3-*.amazonaws.com every s3-<region> spelling. An entry with untrusted refuse is never reached over TLS from a machine that does not trust the cell CA (the image builder): it can take writes, and only the inspected tier keeps them out. An entry with build passthrough is a read-only package or download CDN with no write API: an image build, whose RUN steps do not trust the cell CA, reaches it uninspected; every other host is refused to a build (an owner may give the build full access). A change is a PR a security code owner approves; a recommended version, once shipped, never changes: a new one is a new number.",
